usage: rebis.ligand [--pdb PDB] [--pdb-file PDB_FILE] [--active ACTIVE]
                    [--auto-active] [--top-n TOP_N] [--cutoff CUTOFF]
                    [--proximity PROXIMITY]
                    [--bottleneck-bias BOTTLENECK_BIAS] [--improved] [--json]
                    [--verbose] [--help] [--file FILE] [--stdin]

PDB-aware ligand design from catalytic sites

options:
  --pdb PDB             PDB ID to fetch and analyze
  --pdb-file PDB_FILE   Local PDB file path
  --active ACTIVE       Comma-separated active site residues (e.g.
                        Glu35,Asp52)
  --auto-active         Auto-detect active site residues by proximity
  --top-n TOP_N         Number of top residues for auto-detection
  --cutoff CUTOFF       Distance cutoff for auto-active detection (Å)
  --proximity PROXIMITY
  --bottleneck-bias BOTTLENECK_BIAS
  --improved            Use improved PDB parsing method
  --json                Output as JSON
  --verbose             Verbose output
  --help, -h            Show help
  --file FILE, -f FILE  Input file (JSON or FASTA/sequence)
  --stdin, -i           Read JSON arguments from stdin
  [catalog] Expanded from 10 to 119 proteins (+109 from expanded catalog)
